    "description": "S1-S3 retain private consent and separate actual-host acceptance. S2 now distinguishes completed credential/token exchange from a deadline with unknown outcome; a consumed grant or submitted key is never replayed automatically.",
    "implementation": "Reviewed production Public/Private audit-inside-budget routes,75ms finite32-worker/8MiB boundary and credentialForm request-context save. A real SSE data acknowledgement preserves live subscription semantics; empty headers/comments cannot bypass the deadline. FormHTML locks an ambiguous submitted key and directs fresh setup/state inspection.",
    "tests": "Read held-auth-lock coverage for register/authorize/token/revoke/mcp/private approve, delayed finite proxy/FIFO mapping, consumed refresh single-use, normal local setup and canceled single-submission tests. Isolated fixtures classify normal success and125ms deadline rejection separately. Handler fixtures do not execute the local form browser or establish real-host setup; those gaps remain. Cycle2F2 additionally derives route completeness from actual gateway and artifact source registrations, times GET and HEAD at root and nonempty public prefix including RFC metadata aliases, verifies body/metadata identities and accepted webhook proxy response. Cycle2F4 requires later real stream data and disconnect cancellation, rather than merely sleeping after the acknowledgement. The actual SDK listen handshake fixture consumes a complete acknowledgement frame, then verifies the live stream survives beyond125ms before caller cancellation and requires prompt reader/worker termination. The100ms sample covers only the initial acknowledgement."
